0, "depth": 1, "p_idx": 1, "pred": "[Relevant]The city of Albany is the capital of New York State and is located in Albany County.[No support / Contradictory][Utility:5]</s>", "processed_pred": "[Relevant]The city of Albany is the capital of New York State and is located in Albany County.[No support / Contradictory][Utility:5]</s>", "beam_score": 1.1603875621120632, "ctx": {"title": "Dutch Empire", "text": "of the States\"). The last Director-General of the colony of New Netherland, Pieter Stuyvesant, has bequeathed his name to a street, a neighborhood and a few schools in New York City, and the town of Stuyvesant. Many of the towns and cities along the Hudson in upstate New York have placenames with Dutch origins (for example Yonkers, Hoboken, Haverstraw, Newburgh, Staatsburg, Catskill, Kinderhook, Coeymans, Rensselaer, Watervliet). Nassau County, one of the four that make up Long Island, is also of Dutch origin. The Schuylkill river that flows into the Delaware at Philadelphia is also a Dutch name meaning hidden or"}, "final_score": 1.1603875621120632, "relevance_score": 0.9207896682831526, "ground_score": 0.2395978938289105, "utility_score": 0.0, "seq_score": -0.4445058751212703, "relevance_probs": {"[Irrelevant]": 0.07914603109180264, "[Relevant]": 0.9200421982256223}, "support_probs": [{"[Fully supported]": 0.06551555511362125, "[Partially supported]": 0.34596931878611176, "[No support / Contradictory]": 0.583933786487085}], "utility_probs": [{"[Utility:1]": 0.0005202122925339836, "[Utility:2]": 0.0006811402507174427, "[Utility:3]": 0.0004963900372550406, "[Utility:4]": 0.019444717787921784, "[Utility:5]": 0.7587239988331329}], "n_tokens": 24}, {"node_id": 3, "parent": 0, "depth": 1, "p_idx": 2, "pred": "[Relevant]Alphabet City is a neighborhood located within the East Village in the New York City borough of Manhattan.[Fully supported][Continue to Use Evidence]Its name comes from Avenues A, B, C, and D, the only avenues in Manhattan to have single-letter names.[Continue to Use Evidence]It is bordered by Houston Street to the south and by 14th Street to the north, along the traditional northern border of the East Village and south of Stuyvesant Town and Peter Cooper Village.[Utility:5]</s>", "processed_pred": "[Relevant]Alphabet City is a neighborhood located within the East Village in the New York City borough of Manhattan.[Fully supported][Continue to Use Evidence]Its name comes from Avenues A, B, C, and D, the only avenues in Manhattan to have single-letter names.[Continue to Use Evidence]It is bordered by Houston Street to the south and by 14th Street to the north, along the traditional northern border of the East Village and south of Stuyvesant Town and Peter Cooper Village.[Utility:5]</s>", "beam_score": 1.9383520452637666, "ctx": {"title": "Alphabet City, Manhattan", "text": "Alphabet City, Manhattan Alphabet City is a neighborhood located within the East Village in the New York City borough of Manhattan. Its name comes from Avenues A, B, C, and D, the only avenues in Manhattan to have single-letter names. It is bordered by Houston Street to the south and by 14th Street to the north, along the traditional northern border of the East Village and south of Stuyvesant Town and Peter Cooper Village. Some famous landmarks include Tompkins Square Park and the Nuyorican Poets Cafe. The neighborhood has a long history, serving as a cultural center and ethnic enclave"}, "final_score": 1.9383520452637666, "relevance_score": 0.9981030803262296, "ground_score": 0.940248964937537, "utility_score": 0.0, "seq_score": -0.04988516237816015, "relevance_probs": {"[Irrelevant]": 0.0018965093823909128, "[Relevant]": 0.9978871971260539}, "support_probs": [{"[Fully supported]": 0.9121556021501102, "[Partially supported]": 0.04401632485164175, "[No support / Contradictory]": 0.03735616971674833}], "utility_probs": [{"[Utility:1]": 0.00034807824301491904, "[Utility:2]": 0.0007952043818901017, "[Utility:3]": 0.00033343853340986974, "[Utility: